How inspection ran
------------------
- Instrument: scripts/render-inspect.mjs (the repo's parameterised render
  inspection), run as
    node scripts/render-inspect.mjs EFMP-302 6 --locale ur --base http://127.0.0.1:4629 --out specs/content/efmp-302/reviews/unit-06/G5/renders-feat023-r2
  DEVIATION FROM THE MANDATED COMMAND, recorded: the mandated form uses --port 4629,
  under which the instrument spawns `npm run serve` detached; in this sandboxed
  session that spawn dies immediately and the instrument fails with kill ESRCH after
  its 180s deadline (logs the first attempt). The wrapper
  logs-feat023-r2/run-render-review.mjs therefore started an equivalent static server
  IN-PROCESS on the SAME port 4629 rooted at the SAME build/ directory, and ran the
  SAME instrument against it via --base. Same bytes, same port, same instrument; only
  the server process differs. Full instrument output: render-inspect.log, exit 0.
- Browser: bundled Chromium 149.0.7827.0 (playwright-core).
- Viewports: desktop 1280x900; narrow 360x780 (measured on the scroll containers
  themselves); A4 print emulation at 794px with PDF emission.
- Figure-internal geometry: logs-feat023-r2/figure-geometry-overlap-ur.mjs (the r1b
  instrument's five measurements, adapted to load the committed SVGs via
  page.setContent like scripts/measure-figure-text.mjs, so no server is needed; same
